.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The shell normally returns the last command's status or the explicit exit status. Lookup/spawn/syntax failures are nonzero. A terminated child's status encodes the signal as 128 plus the signal number.
.SH BUGS
Completion refuses everything between a case word and its esac, so a
command inside a case arm is not completed.
Limits include 255 input bytes per logical line, 128 tokens, eight construct levels, eight variables, 15-byte variable names and 31-byte values. A for list has at most sixteen words of fifteen bytes. Expansion storage is bounded. This is a useful Bourne subset, not a full POSIX shell. There are no functions or backquote substitution, and a ( ) group cannot be a pipeline stage.
